# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Rust / Tauri build artifacts
/src-tauri/target
/src-tauri/gen/schemas

# Standalone test build the owner launches directly (RAWY-35) — a copy of the release binary
/test-build/

# Env
.env
.env.*

# Private — working notes that used to live here. They now live outside the repository and
# must stay there; this rule remains as a backstop so a stray copy can never be committed.
/PROJECT.md

# NOTE: `/docs/` is deliberately NOT ignored. It is reserved for the published project site
# (GitHub Pages serves from `docs/` on the default branch). Nothing else belongs in it —
# design sources, screenshots and reports are not repository material.

# RESILIENCE-1 / WP-0 — test artefacts.
#
# Generated EPUB fixtures: rebuilt by `npm run fixtures:build`. The GENERATOR is the source of
# truth and is committed; the binaries are not, so a public repo carries no opaque test blobs.
/tests/fixtures/epub/
#
# The regression CORPUS is real books — mostly third-party copyrighted works, ~55 MB. It lives
# OUTSIDE this repository at %SARD_CORPUS% (default M:\ProjectDocs\sard\Corpus). Only
# tests/corpus/corpus.manifest.json is committed. This rule is a backstop in case anyone ever
# copies the books in: publishing them would be a licensing violation, and irreversible.
/tests/corpus/books/
/corpus/

# Byte-identity failure dumps (FINDING-2). The baselines beside them ARE kept — they are the
# reference. These are per-failure evidence: timestamped, sometimes large, and they name corpus
# books, which are third-party copyrighted works this public repo must never describe in bulk.
/tests/harness/fingerprints/diff-*.json
/tests/harness/subsystem-runs/

# The production-build check's scratch tree (`scripts/verify-main-buildable.mjs`). It extracts the
# tree that would become `main` and builds it, and it must live inside the repository because Node and
# Vite resolve `node_modules` by walking UP from the project directory. Removed on every exit path;
# this rule is the backstop for a run that is interrupted.
/.release-check/

# Sample clips for the background-media harnesses (`bg-media-benchmark`, `bg-media-readability`).
# Tens of MB of video and GIF, generated or downloaded per investigation and never worth committing.
# The harnesses take the directory as `--media=<dir>` or `$SARD_MEDIA_DIR` and fall back to here, so
# this rule keeps that fallback from ever dirtying the working tree.
/tests/harness/.media/

# Private — REAL user data. Each `.db-snapshot-*` directory is a byte copy of the live
# %APPDATA%/com.sard.app/sard.db (+ its -wal/-shm), taken before a risky task. They hold the
# owner's library paths, reading positions, highlights, notes, bookmarks, tags and listening
# records. They were NOT matched by any rule above, so a `git add -A` before the repo goes public
# would publish all of it irreversibly. NEVER pushed.
/.db-snapshot-*/
/.zcode/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# NOTHING ARCHIVED MAY LIVE IN public/. Vite copies public/ verbatim into dist/, and Tauri embeds
# dist/ into the executable — so a stray archive here is compiled into every build. A 47 MB RAR of a
# previous Beta package sat here from 2026-08-05 and tripled the binary (24 MB -> 72 MB) in every
# artifact built afterwards, including one sent to a tester. Nothing referenced it.
public/**/*.rar
public/**/*.zip
public/**/*.7z
public/**/*.exe
public/**/*.msi
